# CLI Task Manager

A professional command-line task management application with natural language processing capabilities.

## Features

- **Natural Language Input**: Create tasks using natural language like "remind me to review PRs every Monday"
- **Smart Parsing**: Automatically extracts dates, priorities, tags, and recurrence patterns
- **Recurring Tasks**: Support for complex recurring patterns
- **Reminders**: Desktop notifications and background daemon
- **Projects & Tags**: Organize tasks with projects and hierarchical tags
- **Dependencies**: Task dependencies and blocking relationships
- **Statistics**: Comprehensive reporting and productivity insights
- **Cross-Platform**: Works on Windows, macOS, and Linux

## Quick Start

### Installation

```bash
pip install cli-task-manager
```

### Basic Usage

```bash
# Add a task
task add "call mom tomorrow at 3pm"

# List tasks
task list

# Complete a task
task complete 1

# Show help
task --help
```

## Natural Language Examples

The parser understands various natural language patterns:

```bash
# Simple tasks
task add "buy milk"
task add "review code"

# With dates
task add "call dentist next Tuesday"
task add "submit report by Friday 5pm"
task add "meeting in 2 hours"

# With priorities
task add "urgent: fix production bug"
task add "high priority: deploy feature X"

# With tags
task add "buy groceries with tags shopping, personal"
task add "review PRs #work #urgent"

# Recurring tasks
task add "weekly team meeting every Monday at 10am"
task add "water plants every 3 days"
task add "monthly report on the 15th"

# With projects
task add "deploy feature in project mobile-app"
task add "review design for project website-redesign"
```

## Commands

### Task Management
- `task add <input>` - Add task with natural language
- `task list [filters]` - List tasks with optional filters
- `task complete <id>` - Mark task as complete
- `task delete <id>` - Delete a task
- `task edit <id>` - Edit task interactively
- `task search <query>` - Search tasks
- `task show <id>` - Show detailed task information

### Projects
- `task project list` - List all projects
- `task project create <name>` - Create project
- `task project archive <name>` - Archive project

### Tags
- `task tag list` - List all tags
- `task tag rename <old> <new>` - Rename tag
- `task tag merge <from> <into>` - Merge tags

### Reminders
- `task remind <id> <when>` - Add reminder to task
- `task snooze <id> <duration>` - Snooze reminder

### Statistics
- `task stats [period]` - Show statistics
- `task report [type]` - Generate report

### Configuration
- `task config show` - Show current configuration
- `task config set <key> <value>` - Update configuration

### Backup
- `task backup create` - Create backup
- `task backup restore <file>` - Restore from backup

### Daemon
- `task daemon start` - Start background daemon
- `task daemon stop` - Stop daemon
- `task daemon status` - Check daemon status

## Configuration

Configuration is stored in `~/.task-manager/config.yaml`. Key settings include:

- Default priority for new tasks
- Notification preferences
- Display settings
- Backup configuration
- Parser settings

## Data Storage

All data is stored locally in `~/.task-manager/`:
- `tasks.db` - SQLite database with all tasks
- `config.yaml` - Configuration file
- `backups/` - Automatic backups
- `logs/` - Application logs

## Development

### Setup Development Environment

```bash
git clone https://github.com/cli-task-manager/cli-task-manager.git
cd cli-task-manager
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

### Running Tests

```bash
pytest
```

### Code Formatting

```bash
black cli_task_manager tests
isort cli_task_manager tests
```

